st  two years  but in 2019 christopher prestopino was a  no-show  he's accused of killing a woman and  dumping her body in the desert  he posted a 500-thousand dollar bond  police found him at his house while he  was supposed to be in court  and took him back to jail it took the  wind out of the sales of  all of us thinking that this is the one  who meets the criteria for house arrest  the i-team examined court records to  find out whether  certain judges were more likely to grant  bail house arrest or electronic  monitoring  for defendants charged with murder and  we found  no major trends i think now we're  finally  equaling the scales of justice because  we have judges who understand the law we  will continue to  investigate these crimes what happens  afterwards  needs to be in my opinion needs to be  looked at and maybe reconsidered  wolfson says a defendant out of custody  can sometimes delay a case  if a defendant isn't in jail he says  their legal team may not hesitate in  asking for continuances  veronica melton says she's been waiting  more than three years  for justice but the action and the  result is still the same  i still have a dead child vanessa murphy  8 news now  in one case our i-team found bail was  reduced for the defendant because of the  coronavirus  according to court records though he has  asthma metro police say as of thursday  15  inmates have kova 19 and were in  isolation deputy chief chavez who you  heard from there  insists there is room for defendants  charged with murder to be safely housed  metro reports 36 vacancy  the second impeachment trial meanwhile  of donald trump is underway in  washington d.c  house managers have argued the capital  attack cost taxpayers millions of  dollars but more importantly  has compromised american national  security washington d.c correspondent  alexander limon reports good evening and  once again today the house impeachment  managers played videos  including some of their fellow lawmakers  rememberi